tasks.detail:
Depends on G1 (G4 for logs/orchards). Trees are the most-repeated art in the frame; base-woods currently reads as bubble wrap because each tree is one circle + one highlight circle + a dark stroke.

(a) `src/render/canopy.ts`: `export function canopySprite(family: 0 | 1 | 2, variant: number, band: number, d: Detail): HTMLCanvasElement` — 3.0 m canvas (fits r≤1.0 plus lobes plus the SE shadow), cached through `stamps.ts`. Content, all in meters, all randomness from `hash(variant, family, salt)`:
1. cast shadow — 6 lobes of `rgba(10,16,8,0.28)` offset by `shadowOffset(0.45)` ≈ (+0.29,+0.35) (matches today's ellipse offset feel);
2. dark silhouette — the mass lobes drawn once at 1.06× scale in `rgba(0,0,0,0.22)`, giving a clean rim for the price of one extra pass (cheaper and less busy than stroking 8 circles);
3. mass — 6-8 lobe circles, r 0.34-0.58·R, centers 0.30-0.50·R from the middle at `i/n*2π + jitter`, filled `shade(CANOPY_A|CANOPY_B, 0.86..1.05)` → ragged, non-circular outline;
4. SE shade — 3 lobes on the SE side, `rgba(14,22,12,0.22)`;
5. NW highlight — 4 lobes `rgba(190,214,148,0.16)` plus 2 small brighter `rgba(206,224,158,0.22)`;
6. gap flecks — 8 dots 0.05-0.09 m `rgba(12,20,10,0.30)`;
7. `d >= 2` only: trunk hint at the SE base (0.09 m dark stub) + 2 short branch strokes.
Families 0/1 = the two woods greens, family 2 = orchard (smaller, rounder, lighter). 12 variants each.

(b) `drawTree` becomes one blit: `const k = r / 0.75; g.drawImage(canopySprite(fam, (hash(x,y,45)*12)|0, band, d), cx - 1.5*k, cy - 1.5*k, 3*k, 3*k);` — replaces ~6 path ops (≈8 µs) with ≈1.3 µs, so a dense woods chunk gets FASTER while looking far better. Keep the existing interior-only canopy-gap cull exactly as is (edge trees must stay, per the sweep finding).

(c) Orchard read: a `woods` tile with no orthogonal woods neighbor but woods at (x±2,y) or (x,y±2) is orchard-planted (mapgen's staggered 2-spacing) → family 2, plus a 0.55 m bare-earth ring `rgba(120,102,70,0.20)` under it and, at `d >= 2`, 3-4 fruit specks ≤0.05 m in muted `rgba(150,74,54,0.50)` (keep tiny — a validator already once mistook red garrison dots for fruit).

(d) Woods floor: replace the 4 per-tile litter ellipses with a `woods:litter:${v}` 1 m stamp (8 variants) — 10 leaf flecks 0.06-0.11 m in `rgba(20,24,14,0.22)` / `rgba(120,110,70,0.16)`, 3 twig strokes 0.15-0.30 m, 1 root arc; at `d >= 2` add fern fronds (3 strokes from a point) and a moss patch `rgba(74,92,56,0.18)`. Blit at `d >= 1`; keep `drawSubTileGround` as the value base.

(e) Fallen logs from the PatchIndex (G4): per woods patch, `n = Math.max(1, patch.tiles / 45)` logs at tiles chosen deterministically from `patch.seed`; a log is a 1.4-2.2 m capsule `#3a2f22` with a NW-lit top strip `rgba(176,158,116,0.30)`, an AO ellipse under it, and 3 stub branches. Drawn in the tree pass so canopy overlaps them.

(f) Hedge depth in `drawHedgeRun` (keep the whole-run layer architecture — it is what fixed segmentation): dab count by tier (d0: 0, d1: 3, d2: 6); push 2 of the dabs onto the silhouette by offsetting them perpendicular to the run by ±width/2 so the outline goes ragged instead of a smooth capsule; add an earth-bank pass BEFORE the green mass — stroke the same `hedgePath` in `rgba(72,58,38,0.35)` at `width*1.25` offset (+0.06,+0.08), plus a 0.05 m dark contact line at the SE foot (bocage hedges sit on a bank; this is what makes them read as bank + foliage rather than a green sausage). At `d >= 2` add 3-4 bare twig strokes at run ends/gates.
